> Hi @simonguinot . Speaking on behalf of my colleague @IVandeVeire (who's currently sick at home), this PR does not fix our issue. The logic high level resulting from the boot sequence is still misinterpreted as the first part of a data bit (as described in [66372](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/issues/66372)) .

Hi @javlands Thanks for your quick reply.

@bjarki-trackunit, I think that the high to low level edge due to the preamble is still interpreted as a bit by the first WS2812 controller of the strip. And all the following bits are shifted. That's the concern I tried to express with my first comment and I don't understand why you are not observing this behavior too.
